{
  "schema": "faktor.compat.sdk-traces/v1",
  "sdk": {
    "commit": "fa02955bfa17b60e57e0d7406d200a73337472ee",
    "package": "@kilocode/sdk",
    "path": "packages/sdk/js",
    "version": "7.5.6"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "args": {
        "full": "true",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.diff",
      "id": "session.diff.content",
      "note": "Exact pass: the replay now carries REAL checkpoint content (the checkpoint probe tool wrote a per-process gitignored scratch file under target/ through the workspace handle and recorded the missing-to-existing transition in the CAS-backed checkpoint store), so ?full=true projects the recorded change with its real unified diff AND the SDK-required additions/deletions counts, counted from that same diff. The path is a test-fixture path, golden-normalized to @string via the driver's probePath var; an empty projection would satisfy Array<SnapshotFileDiff> trivially, so this step asserts the content branch.",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/session/@string/diff",
        "query": "full=true"
      },
      "response": {
        "body": [
          {
            "additions": 1,
            "deletions": 0,
            "diff": "+compat probe",
            "path": "@string",
            "status": "added"
          }
        ],
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#nonempty"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDiffResponses.200 (Array<SnapshotFileDiff>)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "full": "false",
        "messageID": "999",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.diff",
      "id": "session.diff.missing-message",
      "note": "Exact pass (error surface): an unknown messageID answers the SDK-declared 400 BadRequestError {name:'BadRequest',data:{message,kind:'Query'}} \u2014 SessionDiffErrors declares exactly 400 and no other class, so the refusal IS the SDK contract. The 200 content branch (with real checkpoint rows and SDK-required additions/deletions counts) is covered by the session.diff.content step that precedes this one.",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/session/@string/diff",
        "query": "full=false&messageID=999"
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "Query",
            "message": "diff: unknown message id 999"
          },
          "name": "BadRequest"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 400
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "name",
        "data.message"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDiffErrors.400 (BadRequestError)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.abort",
      "id": "session.abort",
      "note": "Exact pass: the SDK declares 200: boolean. The daemon reports whether the abort actually cancelled at least one tracked operation (this trace's just-finished turn still owns one, so true); a fully idle session honestly answers false, never a fabricated success.",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/abort",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": true,
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionAbortResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "messageID": "$cursor",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.revert",
      "id": "session.revert",
      "note": "Exact pass: with the snapshot store wired and a real checkpoint recorded before the newest message, the handler rolls the file back through the CAS-verified rollback path and answers the SDK Session8 rich session projection with the durable revert marker revert: {messageID (the request's own target, echoed), workspace: \"restored\"}. The rollback also stamps checkpoint.restored_ms, which is the durable state unrevert reads.",
      "request": {
        "body": {
          "messageID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/revert",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "createdMs": "@int",
          "directory": ".",
          "id": "@string",
          "model": {
            "id": "m",
            "providerID": "fake"
          },
          "projectID": "@string",
          "revert": {
            "messageID": "@string",
            "workspace": "restored"
          },
          "sessionID": "@string",
          "slug": "@string",
          "state": "ready_for_next_turn",
          "time": {
            "created": "@int",
            "updated": "@int"
          },
          "title": "wire trace updated",
          "updatedMs": "@int",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "workspaceID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "id",
        "revert.messageID",
        "revert.workspace"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionRevertResponses.200 (Session8)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.unrevert",
      "id": "session.unrevert",
      "note": "Exact pass: the SDK sends NO body; the target IS the durable revert state (the newest checkpoint carrying restored_ms, written by rollback and cleared by redo). The handler redoes it through the same CAS-verified path and answers the SDK Session9 rich session projection with no `revert` object (the revert state is gone, never a stale marker).",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/unrevert",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "createdMs": "@int",
          "directory": ".",
          "id": "@string",
          "model": {
            "id": "m",
            "providerID": "fake"
          },
          "projectID": "@string",
          "sessionID": "@string",
          "slug": "@string",
          "state": "ready_for_next_turn",
          "time": {
            "created": "@int",
            "updated": "@int"
          },
          "title": "wire trace updated",
          "updatedMs": "@int",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "workspaceID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "id",
        "time.created"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionUnrevertResponses.200 (Session9)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "messageID": "$cursorUser",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.deleteMessage",
      "id": "session.deleteMessage",
      "note": "Exact pass: a dependency-free message is removed durably and the SDK-declared boolean true is answered. The driver targets the page's user message (captured from session.messages.before) because the daemon refuses deleting the ACTIVE turn's newest message with 409 \u2014 the case the SDK itself declares as SessionBusyError.",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/session/@string/message/@string",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": true,
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDeleteMessageResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "messageID": "$cursor",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.fork",
      "id": "session.fork",
      "note": "The SDK's optional {messageID} body is accepted (the daemon forks the whole history). Exact pass: the response now serves the rich SDK Session5 fields (id, slug, projectID, workspaceID, directory, model, version, time) additively next to the frozen aliases (sessionID, title, createdMs).",
      "request": {
        "body": {
          "messageID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/fork",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "createdMs": "@int",
          "directory": ".",
          "id": "@string",
          "model": {
            "id": "m",
            "providerID": "fake"
          },
          "projectID": "@string",
          "sessionID": "@string",
          "slug": "@string",
          "state": "idle",
          "time": {
            "created": "@int",
            "updated": "@int"
          },
          "title": "wire trace updated (fork)",
          "updatedMs": "@int",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "workspaceID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "id",
        "time.created"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionForkResponses.200 (Session5)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.delete",
      "id": "session.delete",
      "note": "Exact pass: a session whose turn FINISHED (parked ReadyForNextTurn, no active turn record) is durably Closed and the SDK-declared boolean true is answered. The session layer's active-state predicate covers the parked machine, so the compat route completes the close through the daemon's own durable end path (the one /global/dispose uses); a genuinely mid-turn session still refuses 409. The SDK delete contract declares only 400/404, so a parked session must be deletable.",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/session/@string",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": true,
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDeleteResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID2"
      },
      "call": "session.delete",
      "id": "session.delete.clean",
      "note": "Exact pass: a never-driven session is durably ended (SessionEnded + lifecycle Closed) and the SDK-declared boolean true is answered; the row stays as a Closed tombstone (no store row-drop API in this slice).",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/session/@string",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": true,
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDeleteResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "passing"
    }
  ]
}
